        },
        {
            "name": "workIntro",
            "label": "Homepage intro paragraph (HTML allowed)",
            "group": "The Work",
            "value": "I use the word <em>work</em> intentionally here. Therapy is many things, and effortful is one of them. It is not easy to sit in places inside ourselves and in emotions we try hard to avoid, to look at things we usually turn away from, to talk with our partner about a topic that has somehow, in some unspoken way, become off-limits. It's hard to believe that a process often described with words like <em>healing</em>, <em>holding space</em>, <em>journey</em>, <em>discovery</em>, <em>growth</em> can also be associated with tears, fear, anxiety, sadness, and grief. Ah, the human experience — full of paradoxes and complexity. Thank goodness I love both of those things!",
            "type": "textarea"
        },
        {
            "name": "workMoreText",
            "label": "Text before the dive-deeper link",
            "group": "The Work",
            "value": "I pull from a few different theories — narrative, psychodynamic, and somatic, all through an attachment framework.",
            "type": "textarea"
        },
        {
            "name": "workDiveLabel",
            "label": "Dive-deeper link text (links to your The Work page; leave empty to hide)",
            "group": "The Work",
            "value": "Explore how each one might show up in our work together →",
            "type": "text"
        },
        {
            "name": "workBeliefsLabel",
            "label": "Beliefs — intro label",
            "group": "The Work",
            "value": "A few of my beliefs in therapy:",
            "type": "text"
        },
        {
            "name": "workBeliefs",
            "label": "Beliefs list (homepage + The Work page)",
            "group": "The Work",
            "type": "repeater",
            "value": [
                {
                    "text": "I believe the process of getting to know ourselves, meeting all parts of ourselves and our stories with compassion, and bringing all we are to our relationships in an authentic, intimate way is one of the most rewarding things we will ever do in life."
                },
                {
                    "text": "I believe therapy is sacred work."
                },
                {
                    "text": "I believe we need humor in life and also the therapy room."
                },
                {
                    "text": "I believe that when our relationship with our partner feels secure, loving, and embracing, we can face almost anything in life. When our relationship feels like we're walking on eggshells and covered in tension, the rest of our lives feels like crap too."
                },
                {
                    "text": "I believe that people are complex and inherently good."
                }
            ],
            "maxCount": -1,
            "hasEmptyState": true,
            "translations": {
